# Notes
notes = "(!) sega_101.bin (md5): f273555d7d91e8a5a6bfd9bcf066331c|(!) sega_100.bin (md5): 2aba43c2f1526c5e898dfe1cafbfc53a|Built on Ymir's cycle-accurate hardware layer.|Saturn games need one Saturn BIOS ROM in the system directory; any of the listed files works (Japanese v1.00/v1.01 included).|BIOS Auto boots a Japan/Asia-only disc with a Japanese BIOS and any other disc with a US/EU one (falls back to any BIOS present); keep one of each region.|Load .bin/.img/.mdf images through their .cue/.ccd/.mds sheet.|Optional Vulkan renderer (64-bit desktop and Android builds): set the video driver to vulkan, then core option Renderer = Vulkan and reload the content; Internal Resolution 2x-4x (desktop only; Android is 1x) and VDP1 Upscaling apply at once. Other video drivers use the software renderer.|Save states are deterministic: run-ahead, rewind and netplay work. Save states carry the BIOS language/settings for the session. For netplay, use the same BIOS, core options and cheats on both machines.|Cheats: the Saturn cheat files of RetroArch's database (Action Replay codes) work. RetroAchievements and cheat search use Beetle Saturn's memory layout.|Controllers per port: Control Pad, 3D Control Pad, Arcade Racer, Mission Stick, Shuttle Mouse, Virtua Gun; analog deadzone, trigger deadzone and mouse sensitivity options.|The King of Fighters '95 and Ultraman need their ROM cartridge dump in the system directory (mpr-18811-mx.ic1, mpr-19367-mx.ic1).|Optional CD Block LLE (work in progress in Ymir) needs the CD Block ROM (cdb106.bin, cdb105.bin or cdb104.bin) in the system directory; tested with cdb106.bin and cdb105.bin.|ST-V arcade games: load the MAME zip of bakubaku, colmns97, puyosun, diehard, gaxeduel, cotton2, grdforce, rsgun, shienryu, ffreveng, sss, sanjeon or decathlt (thirteen games). They need one ST-V BIOS for the game's regions in the system directory (epr-20091.ic8 Japan, epr-17952a.ic8 USA, epr-17954a.ic8 Europe, or MAME's other names for them) and no Saturn BIOS. Select = Coin, Start, L3 = Service, R3 = Test; saves go to <set>.srm (32,901 bytes; a 0.10.0 .srm of 32,896 bytes still loads).|Screen Rotation (TATE) defaults to Auto: vertical ST-V games (Shienryu) are turned upright and Saturn games are never rotated. If you ran 0.10.0 your saved setting is None: choose Auto, or Shienryu comes up on its side.|Archived Saturn disc images (.zip, .7z) are not supported (a .zip is read only as an ST-V ROM set, and the core asks RetroArch not to unpack archives); extract them or convert them to CHD.|sega1003.bin (JP v1.003) is not supported due to compatibility issues.|Visit https://github.com/coredds/brimir for more information."

description = "Brimir is a libretro core for Sega Saturn and Sega ST-V emulation, built on Ymir's cycle-accurate hardware layer. Features SIMD-optimized threaded software rendering, an optional Vulkan renderer (VDP1 and VDP2 on the GPU, identical to software at native resolution, internal resolution up to 4x on desktop, 1x on Android; needs RetroArch's Vulkan video driver), live core option updates, dynamic NTSC/PAL AV timing, screen rotation (TATE), compressed save states that keep run-ahead, rewind and netplay exact, Action Replay cheats from RetroArch's database, RetroAchievements (Beetle Saturn's memory layout), all Saturn controller types (3D Control Pad, Arcade Racer, Mission Stick, Shuttle Mouse, Virtua Gun with crosshair), RAM, ROM and backup memory cartridges, Ymir's accuracy options (SH-2 cache, CD Block LLE, SCSP step granularity), multi-disc support and thirteen ST-V arcade games (MAME ROM sets). Interlaced high-resolution titles can be CPU-bound on slower machines. An SH-2 JIT is available as an experimental, opt-in option. The core requires a Saturn BIOS ROM (an ST-V BIOS for the arcade games) to function."
